{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>When you come to the land of Canaan.</b> It was not said 'when you come' regarding plagues of people and garments, because they were practiced even in the wilderness; but regarding plagues of houses, since they had none in the wilderness, it was said: when you come to the land of Canaan. Another interpretation: because of the excellence of the land of Israel, that the Temple was destined to be within it, it was required to be clean and pure." "<b>And I will place a plague of tzara'at.</b> One may say according to the plain sense: since it warned below, 'you shall surely destroy all the places where the nations served there' — and we do not know in which place they served — therefore the plague comes upon the houses, to make known the place where the Canaanites served there, in order to destroy it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:12:15.480324582Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}